loy, and manage their applications. [Data: Sources (1, 2, 3), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 10, 15))]\n\n## Cloud Connector and Connectivity Services\n\nThe Cloud Connector is a service that enables businesses to connect their on-premise systems to SAP BTP. It provides a range of features, including authentication, authorization, and data encryption. The Cloud Connector is designed to support the secure and reliable transfer of data between on-premise systems and SAP BTP. [Data: Sources (4, 5, 6), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 10, 15))]\n\n## SAP BTP Regions and Availability\n\nSAP BTP provides a range of regions and availability options to support the deployment of applications. The regions include Europe (Frankfurt), US East (VA), and Japan (Tokyo), among others. The availability options include cloud infrastructure, data management, and analytics. [Data: Sources (7, 8, 9), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 10, 15))]\n\n## SAP BTP Security and Compliance\n\nSAP BTP provides a range of security and compliance features to support the deployment of applications. The features include authentication, authorization, and data encryption. The platform is designed to support the secure and reliable transfer of data between on-premise systems and SAP BTP. [Data: Sources (10, 11, 12), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 10, 15))]\n\n## SAP BTP Community and Support\n\nSAP BTP provides a range of community and support features to support the deployment of applications. The features include online documentation, community forums, and support tickets. The platform is designed to support the development of cloud-native applications and provides a range of tools and services to help businesses build, deploy, and manage their applications. [Data: Sources (13, 14, 15), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 10, 15))]", "# SAP BTP Technology Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP BTP's key components focusing on technology, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to uphold technological standards and manage platform risks effectively. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2024.\n\n## SAP Digital Payments Add-On\n\nThe SAP Digital Payments Add-On at SAP BTP plays a pivotal role in providing user interface texts in multiple languages. Their proactive approach helps safeguard SAP BTP against potential language-related pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective language management not only prevents language anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (320), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 02, 23))]\n\n## Deprecation of Weak Client Certificate Chains\n\nThe Deprecation of Weak Client Certificate Chains at SAP BTP ensures that weak client certificate chains are no longer accepted by the platform. This change, announced on January 25, 2024, is crucial in maintaining SAP BTP's security standards and operational legality, especially in managing complex certificates and certificate chains. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high security standards and ethical practices. [Data: Sources (395, 3952), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 25), (2024, 02, 22))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between SAP BTP's technology components, established in 2023, ensures that technological strategies are aligned with regulatory requirements. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with technological compliance strategies at SAP BTP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with technological standards. [Data: Sources (3953, 3954), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 02), (2024, 02, 22))]", "# SAP BTP and Cloud Foundry Runtime Overview as of 2023-2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP BTP and Cloud Foundry Runtime's key components, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to uphold regulatory standards and manage financial risks effectively. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2023-2024.\n\n## Cloud Foundry Runtime Operational Scope\n\nCloud Foundry Runtime at SAP BTP plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating financial risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2023, helps safeguard SAP against potential financial pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents financial anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (3532, 3533), Date_Range ((2023, 01, 01), (2024, 02, 08))]\n\n## SAP BTP Service Operator and Service Manager\n\nThe SAP BTP Service Operator and Service Manager ensure that all SAP BTP operations adhere to the legal standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on service binding secrets and custom formats, noted starting 2024, is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex contracts and corporate agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high legal standards and ethical practices. [Data: Sources (3535, 3536), Date_Range ((2024, 02, 07), (2024, 04, 18))]\n\n## Cloud Connector and Connectivity\n\nCollaboration between the Cloud Connector and Connectivity teams, established in 2023, ensures that risk mitigation strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (3842, 4098), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 16), (2024, 02, 08))]", "# SAP BTP Technology Overview as of November 2023\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP BTP's key components and their relationships, highlighting the importance of interdepartmental collaboration and adherence to regulatory standards. The information is relevant to SAP BTP's operations around mid-2023.\n\n## Deprecation of Weak Client Certificate Chains\n\nSAP BTP plans to harden the security standards on certain properties for client certificates and their certificate chains in November 2023 to further strengthen platform security. This change will result in weak certificates or certificate chains no longer being accepted by the platform. The change will be rolled out gradually, starting with the region br10 on November 29 and the region eu20 on November 30, 2023. All other regions are planned to be updated in January 2024. [Data: Sources (722), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 02), (2023, 11, 02))]\n\n## Removal of .NET, Ruby, and R Buildpacks\n\nThe .NET, Ruby, and R offline buildpacks have been deprecated and are scheduled to be removed from the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment on November 16, 2023. If you want to continue using these buildpacks after their removal, you can use the online community buildpacks by specifying their URLs in the code of your applications. [Data: Sources (723), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 02), (2023, 11, 02))]\n\n## Additional NAT and LB IPs Added to Amazon Web Services Regions\n\nAdditional NAT and Load Balancer (LB) IP addresses were added on SAP BTP regions running on Amazon Web Services (AWS). The following regions are affected by this change: br10 – Brazil (São Paulo), jp10 – Japan (Tokyo), ap10 – Australia (Sydney), ap11 – Asia Pacific (Singapore), ap12 – Asia Pacific (Seoul), ca10 – Canada (Montreal), eu10 – Europe (Frankfurt), eu11 – Europe (Frankfurt), us10 – US East (VA). [Data: Sources (724), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 02), (2023, 11, 02))]\n\n## SAP BTP Service Operator - Fixed SAP Kubernetes Service Binding Specification\n\nThe Secret created for the service binding contains an instance name key in the service instance info section. This key uses the BTP name of the service binding, which is the value of the external_name property in the service binding spec. The external_instance_name key has been removed from the secret. [Data: Sources (725), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 11), (2023, 11, 02))]\n\n## Tomcat version for Java Web Tomcat 8\n\nJava Web Tomcat 8 (runtime version 3.190) has been updated to Tomcat version 8.5.95. The new version contains security fixes. Update your applications to the latest runtime version. [Data: Sources (726), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 02), (2023, 11, 02))]\n\n## Limits for Roles, Role Collections, Trust, and Service Broker Instances\n\nThere are limits that apply when you define roles, role collections, and trust configurations. Furthermore, the number of service broker instances is limited. For more information, see Limits for Technical Artifacts of the SAP Authorization and Trust Management Service. [Data: Sources (727), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 19), (2023, 11, 02))]\n\n## Generative AI Content Assistant (Beta)\n\nYou can now bootstrap your command and generate fully working DevOps and SRE automation flows by using the new generative AI feature integrated into SAP Automation Pilot. This is a beta feature. See Generative AI in SAP Automation Pilot (Beta). [Data: Sources (728), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 02), (2023, 11, 02))]\n\n## New Expression Functions\n\nAutomation Pilot now supports the jq functions sub and gsub. See Dynamic Expression. [Data: Sources (729), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 02), (2023, 11, 02))]\n\n## Application Development in Authorization Management\n\nDevelopers can use the developer tools of administration management. They build their own applications with authorization policies. Administrators assign authorization policies to users, change the rules and attribute values of existing policies, and create new authorization policies. See Configuring Authorization Policies. [Data: Sources (730), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 02), (2023, 11, 02))]\n\n## Customer Documents\n\nTenant administrator can upload terms of use and privacy policy documents, and e-mail templates in Thai, Malay and Vietnamese. See Configuring Terms of Use, Configuring Privacy Policies, and Configuring Email Templates. [Data: Sources (731), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 02), (2023, 11, 02))]", "# SAP BTP Cloud Foundry Runtime and Kyma Environment Overview as of November 2023\n\nThis report provides an overview of the SAP BTP Cloud Foundry Runtime and Kyma environment, highlighting key components, their relationships, and significant updates as of November 2023. The information is relevant to the SAP BTP Cloud Foundry Runtime and Kyma environment's operations and maintenance.\n\n## SAP BTP Cloud Foundry Runtime Security Enhancements\n\nThe SAP BTP Cloud Foundry Runtime has implemented security enhancements, including the hardening of client certificate chains and the removal of weak certificates. This change aims to strengthen platform security and prevent potential vulnerabilities. The update is scheduled to be rolled out gradually, starting with the region br10 on November 29 and the region eu20 on November 30, 2023. All other regions are planned to be updated in January 2024. [Data: Sources (722), Date_Range ((2023, 05, 18), (2023, 11, 02))]\n\n## Removal of .NET, Ruby, and R Buildpacks\n\nThe .NET, Ruby, and R offline buildpacks have been deprecated and are scheduled to be removed from the SAP BTP Cloud Foundry environment on November 16, 2023. Users can continue to use these buildpacks by specifying their URLs in the code of their applications. For more information, see SAP Note 3364781. [Data: Sources (3952, 4029), Date_Range ((2023, 05, 18), (2023, 11, 02))]\n\n## Additional NAT and LB IPs Added to Amazon Web Services Regions\n\nAdditional NAT and Load Balancer (LB) IP addresses were added to SAP BTP regions running on Amazon Web Services (AWS). The following regions are affected by this change: br10, jp10, ap10, ap11, ap12, ca10, eu10, eu11, and us10. Users should update their configuration to adopt the new IP addresses, which may be used at the end of Q1, 2024. [Data: Sources (3953), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 02), (2024, 01, 31))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of December 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key technology components, highlighting their relationships and significant updates as of December 2024. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations and strategic planning.\n\n## ABAP Environment Updates\n\nThe ABAP Environment at SAP has seen significant updates, including the introduction of the Landscape Portal: BYOG Support in Build Product Version App. This update enables Bring Your Own Git (BYOG) software components, making it easier for developers to work with SAP systems. The update is part of SAP's efforts to improve its technology infrastructure and support the growing demand for cloud-based services. [Data: Sources (593), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 02), (2024, 12, 02))]\n\n## Data Attribute Recommendation Availability\n\nData Attribute Recommendation is now available in several Microsoft Azure regions, including Europe (Netherlands) and US East (VA). This update expands the reach of SAP's technology components and enables customers to access its services from a wider geographic area. [Data: Sources (1832), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 02), (2024, 12, 02))]\n\n## Generative AI Hub Updates\n\nThe Generative AI hub has seen significant updates, including the addition of new models and model versions from Anthropic via AWS Bedrock, Open AI, and Vertex AI. These updates enhance the capabilities of SAP's AI-powered services and enable customers to access more advanced AI features. [Data: Sources (1836, 1844, 1845, 1846), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 02), (2024, 12, 01))]\n\n## Integration with Joule\n\nSAP has integrated its technology components with Joule, a conversational AI copilot tool. This integration enables administrators to ask questions and receive replies from connected SAP business systems, improving the efficiency and effectiveness of SAP's operations. [Data: Sources (1842, 1843), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 02), (2024, 12, 02))]\n\n## Continuous Integration and Delivery Updates\n\nSAP Continuous Integration and Delivery can now be consumed in several new regions, including the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia (Dammam) and Australia (Sydney). This update expands the reach of SAP's technology components and enables customers to access its services from a wider geographic area. [Data: Sources (1849), Date_Range ((2024, 11, 29), (2024, 11, 29))]\n\n## Java Server Updates\n\nThe Java Server has seen significant updates, including the introduction of a new Tomcat version for Java Web Tomcat 10. This update improves the security and performance of SAP's Java-based services and enables customers to access more advanced features. [Data: Sources (1850), Date_Range ((2024, 11, 28), (2024, 11, 28))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key technologies, highlighting their core attributes, connections, and noteworthy claims. The information is relevant to SAP's operations around 2024.\n\n## SAP AI Core Operational Scope\n\nSAP AI Core plays a pivotal role in providing AI capabilities to SAP's customers. Their proactive approach, highlighted throughout 2024, helps safeguard SAP against potential technological pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective AI management not only prevents technological anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (425, 426, 445), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]\n\n## Generative AI Hub\n\nThe Generative AI Hub is a key feature of SAP AI Core, providing a platform for customers to access and utilize various AI models. The hub's capabilities, including prompt registry and grounding, have been expanded throughout 2024, making it an essential tool for SAP's customers. [Data: Sources (425, 426, 445), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between SAP's technology departments, established throughout 2024, ensures that technological advancements are aligned with regulatory requirements. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with technological compliance strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (425, 426, 445), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]", "# SAP Technology Updates as of February 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of key updates and changes within SAP's technology landscape as of February 2024. It highlights the importance of these updates in enhancing the company's offerings and improving user experience. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations during this period.\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Upgrade\n\nSAP has upgraded its Cloud Identity Services, enhancing the security and efficiency of user authentication. This upgrade is crucial for maintaining the integrity of SAP's cloud-based systems and ensuring a secure user experience. The upgrade was completed on February 13, 2024, and is now available for use [Data: Sources (545), Date_Range ((2024, 02, 13), (2024, 02, 13))].\n\n## SAP Fiori Migration and Updates\n\nSAP has announced the migration of SAP Fiori jobs to the Cloud Foundry Environment pipeline, starting from March 2024. This change aims to improve the efficiency and reliability of SAP Fiori services. Additionally, SAP has resolved an issue regarding the deployment of SAP Fiori to the ABAP platform without using a Cloud Connector [Data: Sources (3512, 3513), Date_Range ((2024, 02, 13), (2024, 02, 13))].\n\n## Identity Provisioning Enhancements\n\nSAP has introduced enhancements to its Identity Provisioning service, including the ability to subscribe to notification emails for expiring outbound certificates and support for paging of group members and user groups for SAP Ariba Applications [Data: Sources (3514, 3515), Date_Range ((2024, 02, 13), (2024, 02, 20))].\n\n## Kyma Runtime Updates\n\nSAP has updated its Kyma Runtime service, introducing improvements to the Telemetry Manager, resource utilization, and support for running in a 'deny all' Network Policy environment [Data: Sources (3516), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 29), (2024, 02, 13))].\n\n## SAP Build Apps and Datasphere Updates\n\nSAP has introduced new features and updates to its SAP Build Apps and Datasphere services, including improved completion speed of Web builds and new features for administration, data integration, data modeling, and data privacy and protection [Data: Sources (3517, 3518), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 02, 13))].\n\n## UI Theme Designer and Pricing Service Updates\n\nSAP has updated its UI Theme Designer service, introducing new base theming content, and resolved an issue with the Pricing Service regarding engine traces [Data: Sources (3519, 3520), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 02, 13))].", "# SAP Technology Updates as of June 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of key SAP technology updates as of June 2024, highlighting new features, deprecations, and maintenance changes across various components. The information is relevant to SAP's technology landscape and its users.\n\n## End of Mainstream Maintenance for Desktop Agent 2\n\nSAP Build Process Automation has announced the end of mainstream maintenance for Desktop Agent 2, effective June 30, 2024. This change affects users who rely on Desktop Agent 2, and they are recommended to migrate to Desktop Agent 3. The Best Practices for Migration document provides guidance on this process. [Data: Sources (658), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 25), (2024, 06, 25))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Upgrade\n\nCloud Identity Services have been upgraded, providing users with improved functionality and security. This upgrade is part of SAP's ongoing efforts to enhance its technology infrastructure and ensure compliance with regulatory standards. [Data: Sources (2692), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 25), (2024, 06, 25))]\n\n## New Version of SAP Document Management Mobile App\n\nSAP has released a new version of the SAP Document Management mobile app, featuring an enhanced user interface and simplified onboarding experience. This update aims to improve user efficiency and productivity, making it easier to manage documents on-the-go. [Data: Sources (2693), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 25), (2024, 06, 25))]\n\n## Deprecation of SAP Fiori in Cloud Foundry Environment Pipeline\n\nSAP has deprecated the SAP Fiori in the Cloud Foundry Environment pipeline type, replacing it with the Cloud Foundry Environment pipeline type. This change affects users who rely on SAP Fiori, and they are recommended to migrate to the new pipeline type. [Data: Sources (2695), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 24), (2024, 06, 24))]\n\n## Identifier API Decommissioning\n\nSAP has announced the decommissioning of the Identifier API, scheduled for September 2025. Users are recommended to use the Schema API to process paymentAdvice documents in Excel format. This change affects users who rely on the Identifier API, and they should plan for alternative solutions. [Data: Sources (2696), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 24), (2024, 06, 24))]\n\n## New Component Version Available for SAP HANA Cloud\n\nA new component version is available for SAP HANA Cloud, providing users with improved functionality and security. This update is part of SAP's ongoing efforts to enhance its technology infrastructure and ensure compliance with regulatory standards. [Data: Sources (2697), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 25), (2024, 06, 24))]\n\n## Usability and Stability Improvements for Data Attribute Recommendation\n\nSAP has released usability and stability improvements for Data Attribute Recommendation, resolving issues with UTF-8 Byte Order Mark (BOM) encoding type and abandoning AI API executions and deployments that remain in UNKNOWN status for more than 3 and 6 hours, respectively. [Data: Sources (2698), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 24), (2024, 06, 24))]", "# SAP AI and Technology Overview as of June 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's AI and technology components, highlighting key updates, announcements, and improvements across various departments. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations around mid-2025.\n\n## Generative AI Hub Updates\n\nThe Generative AI hub has undergone significant updates, including the deprecation of the Mistralai model and the introduction of new models such as Claude Opus 4 and Claude Sonnet 4. These updates aim to enhance the AI capabilities and improve user experience. The hub now supports prompt shields for input filtering with Azure Content Safety, detecting and mitigating prompt attacks. [Data: Sources (201, 597, 598), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 02), (2025, 06, 23))]\n\n## SAP Document AI Improvements\n\nSAP Document AI has seen improvements in its machine learning model for purchase order documents, enhancing its accuracy and efficiency. Additionally, code and stability improvements have been made to the overall system. These updates aim to improve user experience and operational efficiency. [Data: Sources (591, 592), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 24), (2025, 06, 27))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Upgrade\n\nCloud Identity Services have been upgraded, providing improved security and functionality. The upgrade includes the introduction of new signing certificates, enhancing the overall security of the system. [Data: Sources (594, 595), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 23), (2025, 06, 23))]\n\n## Process Visibility Capability Enhancements\n\nThe Process Visibility Capability has been enhanced with the introduction of navigation links on steps, allowing users to navigate to specific pages for additional details. This update aims to improve user experience and operational efficiency. [Data: Source (596), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 23), (2025, 06, 23))]\n\n## SAP AI Launchpad Updates\n\nSAP AI Launchpad has seen updates, including the introduction of new models such as Claude Opus 4 and Claude Sonnet 4. These updates aim to enhance the AI capabilities and improve user experience. [Data: Sources (597, 599), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 23), (2025, 06, 23))]\n\n## SAP Build Enhancements\n\nSAP Build has been enhanced with the introduction of a new copy feature for actions projects, allowing users to duplicate and reuse actions within their project. This update aims to improve user experience and operational efficiency. [Data: Source (600), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 23), (2025, 06, 23))]", "# SAP Technology Updates as of June 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of key SAP technology updates, highlighting the importance of these changes in enhancing the functionality and efficiency of SAP systems. The updates cover various components, including SAP Document AI, SAP HANA Cloud, Cloud Identity Services, and SAP AI Core, among others. These updates are crucial for maintaining the integrity and operational stability of SAP systems, ensuring they remain aligned with the latest market regulations and standards.\n\n## SAP Document AI Enhancements\n\nSAP Document AI has undergone significant enhancements, including the improvement of the machine learning model for purchase order documents. These updates are essential for improving the accuracy and efficiency of document processing, enabling businesses to make informed decisions based on reliable data. The updates also include the removal of dots in extraction results from standard line item fields for purchase order documents, further enhancing the functionality of SAP Document AI. [Data: Sources (453, 780), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 24), (2025, 06, 27))]\n\n## SAP HANA Cloud Updates\n\nSAP HANA Cloud has received updates, including the availability of new component versions. These updates are crucial for maintaining the integrity and operational stability of SAP HANA Cloud, ensuring it remains aligned with the latest market regulations and standards. The updates also include the introduction of a new component version for SAP HANA Cloud, SAP HANA database, and data lake, further enhancing the functionality and efficiency of SAP HANA Cloud. [Data: Sources (593), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 23), (2025, 06, 27))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Updates\n\nCloud Identity Services have been upgraded, ensuring the security and integrity of user identities. The updates include the introduction of new signing certificates, further enhancing the security of Cloud Identity Services. The updates also include the announcement of the version of the newly created signing certificates, v3, which is essential for maintaining the security and integrity of user identities. [Data: Sources (594, 595), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 23), (2025, 06, 27))]\n\n## SAP AI Core Updates\n\nSAP AI Core has received updates, including the introduction of new generative AI models. These updates are essential for enhancing the functionality and efficiency of SAP AI Core, enabling businesses to make informed decisions based on reliable data. The updates also include the announcement of the support for Anthropic models Claude Opus 4 and Claude Sonnet 4, further enhancing the functionality and efficiency of SAP AI Core. [Data: Sources (597, 598, 599), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 23), (2025, 06, 27))]\n\n## Process Visibility Capability Updates\n\nProcess Visibility Capability has received updates, including the introduction of a new feature for configuring navigation links on steps. These updates are essential for enhancing the functionality and efficiency of Process Visibility Capability, enabling businesses to make informed decisions based on reliable data. The updates also include the announcement of the availability of the new feature, further enhancing the functionality and efficiency of Process Visibility Capability. [Data: Sources (596), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 23), (2025, 06, 27))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime Updates\n\nKyma Runtime has received updates, including the update to version 1.17.3 of the Istio module. These updates are essential for maintaining the integrity and operational stability of Kyma Runtime, ensuring it remains aligned with the latest market regulations and standards. The updates also include the announcement of the fix for a bug that caused Istio Operator to create a new ReplicaSet during each reconciliation of a failing, outdated Pod with a sidecar, further enhancing the functionality and efficiency of Kyma Runtime. [Data: Sources (778), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 26), (2025, 05, 27))]", "# SAP Technology Updates Overview as of 2023\n\nThis report provides an overview of key updates and changes within SAP's technology landscape, focusing on components such as ABAP Environment, Continuous Integration & Delivery, SAP Datasphere, Kyma Runtime, and Integration Suite General Features. The information highlights new features, deprecations, and announcements affecting these components, relevant to SAP's technology operations as of 2023.\n\n## ABAP Environment Updates\n\nThe ABAP Environment has seen updates to the XCO Library, allowing for the addition of new worksheets to existing workbooks. This enhancement is crucial for users working with XLSX modules, enabling more efficient data management and analysis. The update is available in both ABAP Environment 2402 and Cloud versions, ensuring compatibility across different environments. [Data: Sources (779, 780), Date_Range ((2023, 02, 16), (2023, 11, 01))]\n\n## Deprecation of Native Blue-Green Deployment\n\nThe native blue-green deployment in Continuous Integration & Delivery is deprecated and will be removed after October 31st, 2023. Users are advised to choose the standard deploy type for any deployment to Cloud Foundry in the Acceptance and Release stages. This change affects jobs using the build tool node or Maven, requiring updates to configurations and deployment strategies. [Data: Source (3983), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 31), (2023, 10, 31))]\n\n## Deprecation of Node 14 and Node 16 Build Tool Versions\n\nThe Node 14 and Node 16 build tool versions in Continuous Integration & Delivery are deprecated and will be removed after October 31st, 2023. Users are recommended to update their configurations to use Node 18 versions instead. This change affects jobs containing the deprecated build tool versions, requiring updates to ensure compatibility and continued functionality. [Data: Source (3984), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 31), (2023, 10, 31))]\n\n## Features for Version 2023.23\n\nSAP Datasphere has introduced new and changed features for administration, available in version 2023.23. These updates aim to enhance user experience and operational efficiency, providing users with more information and tools for effective administration. The features are now generally available, allowing users to explore and utilize them as needed. [Data: Source (3985), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 31), (2023, 10, 31))]\n\n## Deprecation of Serverless-Registry-Config Secret Handling\n\nThe serverless-registry-config Secret handling in Kyma Runtime is deprecated and will be removed after April 1st, 2024. Users are recommended to configure the Docker registry using the dedicated configuration option in Serverless CR. This change affects users working with serverless-registry-config custom Secrets, requiring updates to ensure continued functionality. [Data: Source (3986), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 30), (2024, 04, 01))]\n\n## Changes in the User Interface\n\nThe user interface in Integration Suite General Features has undergone changes, including the general availability of Edge Integration Cell, renaming of the Integrations tab, and introduction of the Engage section. These updates aim to enhance user experience and provide more information and tools for effective integration and API management. The changes are now generally available, allowing users to explore and utilize them as needed. [Data: Source (3987), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 28), (2023, 10, 28))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's technology landscape, highlighting key components, their relationships, and significant updates. The information is relevant to SAP's operations around 2025.\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Operational Scope\n\nCloud Identity Services at SAP play a pivotal role in managing identities across various environments. Their proactive approach helps safeguard SAP against potential security risks and ensures continuous compliance with evolving security regulations. Effective identity management not only prevents security anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (56, 620), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 11), (2025, 06, 30))]\n\n## Cloud Integration for Data Services Updates\n\nCloud Integration for Data Services at SAP ensures seamless data integration across various platforms. Their focus on supporting Microsoft Managed Identities, noted in 2025, is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex data integrations. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high data standards and security practices. [Data: Source (557), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 20), (2025, 06, 27))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Innovation\n\nCollaboration between various SAP technology components, established in 2024, ensures that innovation strategies are aligned with operational requirements. This synergy is vital for holistic innovation and has been instrumental in integrating various components at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with innovation requirements. [Data: Sources (620, 552), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 14), (2025, 06, 30))]"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_9dc98501c1e74552307f5d2d70d78b4cea06508ffdf12ec54767edd0a2fba534_v2"}